# THE QUARANTINE — master screenplay
#
# This is the human-editable dramatic spine. The granular prose remains in the
# linked text/*.txt corpus; SOURCE records make the whole canon part of this
# script, while LINK records show which material plays on each day.
#
# Grammar: SOURCE path | LINK path | SCENE id day title | BEAT kind | text |
# DIALOGUE speaker | text | BRANCH id | prompt | OPTION id next | label.
# The editor's Game events window writes EVENT id kind day hour | label, followed
# by optional EVENT_SOURCE, EVENT_SPEAKER, EVENT_CUE, EVENT_EFFECT | key=value,
# and EVENT_NEXT scene-id, and EVENT_RANDOM earliest-hour latest-hour records.
# A random range resolves to a stable minute inside the range for each game run.
# These are the game-loop schedule, not prose.
# Branch targets are scene ids or END. Keep ids stable: saves and analytics use them.

SOURCE text/broadcasts/week-1.txt
SOURCE text/broadcasts/week-2.txt
SOURCE text/broadcasts/week-3.txt
