# Bounded loop events consumed by GameEventCursor. Keep IDs stable for saves.
EVENT day-01-wake broadcast 1 7 | Wake and begin the day.
EVENT day-01-threshold visitor 1 10 | The first threshold is available.
EVENT day-02-wake broadcast 2 7 | Wake after the first sleep.
EVENT day-02-consequence aftermath 2 12 | The first consequence settles.
EVENT day-03-beat visitor 3 10 | Day 3 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-04-beat visitor 4 10 | Day 4 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-05-beat visitor 5 10 | Day 5 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-06-beat visitor 6 10 | Day 6 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-07-beat visitor 7 10 | Day 7 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-08-beat visitor 8 10 | Day 8 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-09-beat visitor 9 10 | Day 9 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-10-beat visitor 10 10 | Day 10 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-11-beat visitor 11 10 | Day 11 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-12-beat visitor 12 10 | Day 12 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-13-beat visitor 13 10 | Day 13 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-14-beat visitor 14 10 | Day 14 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-15-beat visitor 15 10 | Day 15 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-16-beat visitor 16 10 | Day 16 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-17-beat visitor 17 10 | Day 17 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-18-beat visitor 18 10 | Day 18 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-19-beat visitor 19 10 | Day 19 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-20-beat visitor 20 10 | Day 20 authored beat becomes available.
EVENT day-21-ending ending 21 20 | Day 21 ending evaluation becomes available.

SCENE day-01 1 Hospitality
LINK text/broadcasts/week-1.txt
LINK text/street.txt
LINK text/visitors/ayling.txt
BEAT action | The house opens on a street still full of ordinary traffic, tea, shopping, drains, and people lending one another small help.
DIALOGUE iris | Iris names Ron casually; Ayling offers the shop and the wall-knock compact begins.
BRANCH day-01-care | How do you meet the first small kindness?
OPTION accept day-02 | Accept tea or help and keep the wall-knock promise.
OPTION refuse day-02 | Refuse politely and keep the distance.

SCENE day-02 2 Family evidence
LINK text/visitors/sibling.txt
LINK text/visitors/nurse.txt
BEAT action | Denise brings pears and three true domestic facts before an over-precise memory. Nurse and Ken establish reliable outside routines.
DIALOGUE denise | The pears are left on the step; the family argument is warm, ordinary, and specific.
BRANCH day-02-pears | What do you do with the pears?
OPTION take day-03 | Take them in and record the visit.
OPTION leave day-03 | Leave them where they are.

SCENE day-03 3 Being useful
LINK text/visitors/child.txt
LINK text/visitors/hazmat-boy.txt
BEAT action | Sylvia wants a pencil for a window map. Ronnie's body does not fit the suit. Prentice still honors an appointment. Askew remains exact.
DIALOGUE sylvia | “I'm Sylvia. Number 3.” The letterbox is the whole relationship, and the impossible second remains unwriteable.
BRANCH day-03-pencil | Do you give Sylvia the pencil?
OPTION give day-04 | Give it through the letterbox.
OPTION keep day-04 | Keep it for the journal.
OPTION none day-04 | Admit you have none.

SCENE day-04 4 Repair
LINK text/visitors/engineer.txt
LINK text/visitors/clerk.txt
LINK text/visitors/twins.txt
BEAT action | Reeve, Liddell, and the Bells each repair a system that is slightly obsolete but still workable. An entry appears in the journal from three days ago.
BRANCH day-04-trace | How close do you let Liddell get to the dead pair?
OPTION trace day-05 | Let him trace it to the wall plate.
OPTION outside day-05 | Keep him outside.

SCENE day-05 5 Ownership of a record
LINK text/visitors/warden.txt
LINK text/visitors/sibling.txt
LINK text/documents.txt
BEAT action | Mrs Hallow asks for an ordinary heirloom. Denise defends privacy. Sowerby needs a box filled and writes in the journal.
DIALOGUE warden | The record is requested as if ownership were an ordinary household courtesy.
BRANCH day-05-record | What do you show?
OPTION all day-06 | Show everything.
OPTION card day-06 | Show the card only.
OPTION refuse day-06 | Refuse.

SCENE day-06 6 Being known
LINK text/visitors/doctor.txt
LINK text/visitors/tuner.txt
LINK text/visitors/gas-man.txt
BEAT action | Marchant asks memory questions without diagnosing. Ronnie repeats the script. Kettering appraises the repaired chair. Ashworth knows the private household.
BRANCH day-06-detail | Do you accept Eileen's first identifying detail?
OPTION accept day-07 | Accept it.
OPTION refuse day-07 | Refuse it without explanation.

SCENE day-07 7 Promises
LINK text/broadcasts/week-1.txt
LINK text/visitors/milkman.txt
LINK text/visitors/nurse.txt
BEAT action | Last milk, a reduced nursing list, held post, and Iris seeking a matching answer close the first act. The normality makes the future entry worse.
BRANCH day-07-promise | Which promise do you keep?
OPTION wall-knock day-08 | Keep the wall knock.
OPTION letter day-08 | Reply to the letter.
OPTION record day-08 | Defend the record.

SCENE day-08 8 Wording travels
LINK text/visitors/child.txt
LINK text/visitors/stranger.txt
LINK text/broadcasts/week-2.txt
BEAT action | The boundary sighting becomes a phrase neighbors carry. Voss shows a harmless version mismatch. Sylvia asks what moved.
BRANCH day-08-word | How do you answer the carried wording?
OPTION cite day-09 | Cite the announcement.
OPTION question day-09 | Question the word “accounted.”
OPTION decline day-09 | Decline to make a claim.

SCENE day-09 9 Performance
LINK text/visitors/ayling.txt
LINK text/visitors/evacuee.txt
LINK text/visitors/sibling.txt
BEAT action | Ayling enjoys correct wording. Reeve delivers the cost of reduced allowance. Corrigan describes billeting. Denise asks for acknowledgment rather than a date.
BRANCH day-09-help | Where do you spend the practical help?
OPTION person day-10 | Help one person.
OPTION supplies day-10 | Preserve time and gas.

SCENE day-10 10 The account
LINK text/visitors/sibling.txt
LINK text/visitors/clerk.txt
LINK text/visitors/engineer.txt
BEAT action | An appointment moves, an obsolete order persists, a copy is trusted, and Denise supplies mutually incompatible sighting facts.
BRANCH day-10-notes | What status does the account receive?
OPTION write day-11 | Write one concrete detail.
OPTION uncertain day-11 | Mark it uncertain.
OPTION omit day-11 | Omit it.

SCENE day-11 11 Categories
LINK text/visitors/census.txt
LINK text/visitors/doctor.txt
LINK text/visitors/hazmat-boy.txt
BEAT action | Wren counts a household. Marchant repeats a bodily sequence. Ronnie cannot say the missing noun. The reliable scar distinction fails.
BRANCH day-11-ronnie | Do you ask the direct question?
OPTION ask day-12 | Ask Ronnie directly.
OPTION suit day-12 | Ask about the suit.
OPTION silence day-12 | Let the script end.

SCENE day-12 12 Circulation
LINK text/visitors/evacuee.txt
LINK text/visitors/nurse.txt
LINK text/visitors/ayling.txt
BEAT action | Corrigan admits she floated the ration guess. Ken attributes it elsewhere. Iris speaks Denise's sentence. Prentice hears the room rather than a piano.
BRANCH day-12-rumour | How do you handle the circulating story?
OPTION confront day-13 | Confront the source.
OPTION protect day-13 | Protect her.
OPTION ordinary day-13 | Treat it as ordinary rumor.

SCENE day-13 13 Mercy in correction
LINK text/visitors/ayling.txt
LINK text/visitors/stranger.txt
LINK text/visitors/warden.txt
BEAT action | Ayling accepts correction so action can continue. Voss preserves both copies. Sowerby needs one version. Ashworth refuses to correct your wrong account of him.
BRANCH day-13-document | Which document do you present?
OPTION helpful day-14 | Present the helpful falsification.
OPTION harmful day-14 | Present the harmful correction.
OPTION both day-14 | Present both and explain the conflict.

SCENE day-14 14 Honest revision
LINK text/visitors/child.txt
LINK text/visitors/sibling.txt
LINK text/visitors/evacuee.txt
BEAT action | Sylvia times the absent word. Corrigan keeps her case packed. Denise arrives with a crossed-out list and admits the coach memory was hers to correct.
DIALOGUE denise | “You were right about the coach to Rhyl.” The emotional climax is honest revision, with no scare interrupting it.
BRANCH day-14-revision | How do you receive the concession?
OPTION accept day-15 | Accept it.
OPTION prosecute day-15 | Keep prosecuting the details.
OPTION pencil day-15 | Offer Denise the pencil.

SCENE day-15 15 Inherited answers
LINK text/visitors/doctor.txt
LINK text/visitors/warden.txt
LINK text/visitors/clerk.txt
BEAT action | Marchant carries forward last week. Sowerby finds boxes already filled. Cole reduces the player to door status.
BRANCH day-15-effort | Do you correct the inherited answer?
OPTION correct day-16 | Correct it.
OPTION conserve day-16 | Conserve effort.

SCENE day-16 16 Who counts as present
LINK text/visitors/engineer.txt
LINK text/visitors/ayling.txt
LINK text/visitors/caller.txt
BEAT action | An unchanged reading, “you saw it,” and a second plate orbit the lit empty house.
BRANCH day-16-fiction | Do you challenge one compassionate fiction?
OPTION challenge day-17 | Challenge it.
OPTION allow day-17 | Allow it to stand.

SCENE day-17 17 Names and objects
LINK text/visitors/ayling.txt
LINK text/visitors/neighbour.txt
LINK text/visitors/twins.txt
BEAT action | Ayling receives the clipboard. Ken carries the unposted parcel. Ashworth returns Eileen's case with one exact journal entry. The Bells abandon the scar test.
DIALOGUE piano | Four distant notes occur twice with ordinary room timing; the house does not explain them.
BRANCH day-17-responsibility | Which responsibility do you accept?
OPTION clipboard day-18 | Accept the clipboard.
OPTION parcel day-18 | Accept the parcel.
OPTION case day-18 | Accept the case.

SCENE day-18 18 Public event, private language
LINK text/visitors/evacuee.txt
LINK text/visitors/hazmat-boy.txt
LINK text/visitors/clerk.txt
BEAT action | The street is full and empty. Ayling has no detail. Ronnie completes his promise to return. Cole logs only the shut door.
BRANCH day-18-ronnie | Does Ronnie risk one unscripted sentence?
OPTION speak day-19 | Let him speak.
OPTION script day-19 | Keep to the script.

SCENE day-19 19 What care repeats
LINK text/visitors/child.txt
LINK text/visitors/sibling.txt
LINK text/nights.txt
BEAT action | Replays carry the journal anomaly. Sylvia has the pencil, Denise has pears or not, and Attercliffe knows she repeated herself. Physical residues remain inspectable while the false replay runs.
BRANCH day-19-return | What do you revisit?
OPTION pencil day-20 | Revisit the pencil.
OPTION pears day-20 | Revisit the pears.
OPTION journal day-20 | Revisit the journal.

SCENE day-20 20 Unfinished business
LINK text/visitors/warden.txt
LINK text/visitors/ayling.txt
LINK text/visitors/stranger.txt
BEAT action | Hallow, Ayling, Sowerby, Attercliffe, and Iris close what can be closed: a dish, a form, a shift, a plate, a brief wall knock.
BRANCH day-20-close | Which ordinary thread reaches closure?
OPTION dish day-21 | Return the dish.
OPTION form day-21 | Finish the form.
OPTION wall day-21 | Answer the wall knock.

SCENE day-21 21 Release
LINK text/endings.txt
LINK text/nights.txt
BEAT action | Cole finishes his sheet. The Board thanks Ayling. No principal arrives to summarize the run.
BEAT action | The ending returns two or three chosen objects and phrases as texture, then stops. It does not explain the sun or the house.
BRANCH day-21-ending | Which authored ending does the recorded run reach?
OPTION compliance END | Compliance: lock the house and sleep.
OPTION rupture END | Rupture: the kitchen is there and wrong.
OPTION synchronisation END | Synchronisation: gather the true entries and let the page end.
